# Line endings, decided once, in the repository rather than per machine.
#
# Without this file every contributor's `core.autocrlf` decides how their working
# copy differs from the stored blob. On this machine it is `true`, which is why
# every commit in this project printed "LF will be replaced by CRLF" and why a
# snapshot uploaded through the GitHub web UI came back showing 116 files changed
# with roughly 54 000 insertions and 54 000 deletions — a whole-file rewrite in
# which not one character of code had actually changed.
#
# `text=auto eol=lf` stores everything as LF and checks it out as LF everywhere.
# Two reasons LF rather than native:
#
#   * The shell scripts in `scripts/` run inside Linux containers. A CRLF shebang
#     line makes the kernel look for `/usr/bin/env bash\r`, and the error it gives
#     ("no such file or directory") names a file that plainly exists — one of the
#     more time-wasting failures available.
#   * PostgreSQL functions in the migrations are stored with their body text. CRLF
#     inside a `$$ ... $$` block is preserved into the catalogue, so two developers
#     on different platforms can produce migrations that differ byte-for-byte while
#     appearing identical.
#
# `.ps1` is the deliberate exception: PowerShell on Windows is the only consumer,
# and CRLF is its native form.

* text=auto eol=lf

*.ps1   text eol=crlf
*.bat   text eol=crlf
*.cmd   text eol=crlf

# Binary — never touched, never diffed as text.
*.png   binary
*.jpg   binary
*.jpeg  binary
*.gif   binary
*.ico   binary
*.pdf   binary
*.zip   binary
*.gz    binary
*.dump  binary

# Generated artefacts. They are committed on purpose — `Cargo.lock` because this
# repository produces a binary and a reproducible dependency set is a security
# requirement, the OpenAPI documents because they are the frozen frontend contract
# — but a reviewer should not have to scroll past them to reach the real change.
Cargo.lock       linguist-generated=true
api/openapi.json linguist-generated=true -diff
api/openapi.yaml linguist-generated=true -diff
